65 runs: reduction order (pairwise, left to right, reversed, 3 random); FMA contraction; Monte Carlo arithmetic (mca, 53 bits, 8 samples)
digits: the leading significant digits that stay the same; `|` marks where they stop

  #  value                    order    fma    mca  stable  printed as
  1  5.00|04445029117051e-13    all    all    3.9     3.9  1 - cos(x)
  2  4.99999999999958|29e-13    all    all   15.4    15.4  2 sin(x/2)^2

which lines move the digits (each line perturbed alone: the most-executed first, then lines traced by bisection)
  digits.viv:5  2 ops  #2 to 15.8 (mca)
      good = 2.0 * s * s
  digits.viv:9  2 ops  moves no printed digit
      assert_true(abs(naive - good) < 1.0e-3 * good)
  digits.viv:3  1 ops  #1 to 3.9 (mca)  (traced from #1)
      naive = 1.0 - cos(x)
